 and makes it harder for Black to develop smoothly.\n\nReason: B: f1-b5 pins the knight on c6 to the king on e8, creating immediate tactical pressure. This forces Black to deal with the pin before proceeding with normal development. It's a principled developing move that creates concrete problems for the opponent while improving my position.\n\nAnswer: B: f1-b5"}
