is on d7, f-pawn on f7)\n- Exerts pressure on Black's position\n- Supports future central pawn advances\n- Prepares potential tactics involving the weak f7 square\n- Centralizes my most active piece\n\nThis move follows classical chess principles: control the center with pieces, especially when you can occupy strong squares that cannot be easily challenged.\n\n**Answer:** N: f3-e5"}
