terial.\n\nReason: Playing d2-d4 is the most principled move. It opens lines for my bishop on c1, controls the center, and creates dynamic possibilities. When significantly behind in material, passive play leads to slow defeat. I need to activate my pieces and create complications. This pawn break is the most forcing and development-oriented option available.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4"}
